    {
      "id": 47654062,
      "title": "Ask HN: Any interesting niche hobbies?",
      "url": "",
      "domain": "",
      "author": "e-topy",
      "score": 447,
      "comments": 676,
      "time": 1775424619,
      "text": "I&#x27;m looking for something novel and interesting, that isn&#x27;t absolutely crowded that I could meaningfully contribute to.<p>In 2022 I was toying around with OpenAI&#x27;s RL Gym, right when the first non-instruct GPT3 model came out. I was thinking about getting into ML a lot more, but hesitated.\nBefore that it was 3D printers, mechanical keyboards, drones, etc.\nAll of these have exploded, and while they are still very interesting, I do love my Browns and manage Prusas for my local hackerspace, they have just, for the lack of a better term, industrialized.\nI&#x27;m also now in a position where I have time and money for it, not like when I was 15 and rating Ender motherboard upgrades I knew I&#x27;d never buy.<p>Right now I&#x27;m making a chess engine, but that&#x27;s already a solved problem.\nThere&#x27;s also biohacking, and while designing chips to go into my body is really interesting, I only have one, and don&#x27;t want to push it too far.\nOne promising idea is a kind of &#x27;Personal Computer 2&#x27;, where people try to innovate HCI, and while I really like that and do have some research ideas, I&#x27;d like to explore a bit more before delving deep into it.",
      "rank": 13,
      "importance_score": 538.6,
      "hn_link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47654062",
      "signal_label": "trending",
      "seen_before": false
